es a power outage, and Paul goes missing; meanwhile the magazineâ€™s jaded editor, Cohen, takes an overdose of barbiturates.</p><p>In alternate chapters a very different tale unfolds, set in a distant medieval world redolent of Norse mythology. A man, referred to only as â€œthe strangerâ€, is nursed back to health by a nine-year-old girl who has shot him with an arrow after mistaking him for a deer. He is being pursued by a vengeful duke, and persuades the girl to join him on the run. Together they leave their plague-ridden town, traverse a&nbsp;barren wasteland and discover a&nbsp;subterranean stone city whose inhabitants live a communal existence, subsisting on seafood and kelp.</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/books/2026/jul/23/air-by-christian-kracht-review-a-metaphysical-jigsaw-puzzle">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;4YxKYTyPYs-AjCya-2c0TAsMxIBI81JbLzDzhuMzBMgƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;0-mWDaRQctTIp3h_xLeG0t9VcuLuGZjG7Kixxp32CWIƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;cHZ46fGQR_gKa0Gvj8E9CMLjaeVIP7FQnbzGnqKccB4ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;4ix98UwdsP1eOoU8VozX4B4dcYR1fJ6eMGdlQj2Qfo0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;NNQjntV_Gqbtu-aKt6c_Fk3lop_0SEQVsz-dN0onpcYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;2OknHRw1DboL3pR-X_k5COMIAjtUojGPVFWtGa6NjA4ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;816wwuctxqbOFT_UCBc98SEkGbJykFvFNLbZlrzuMowƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒeri